Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:47:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A panic names its file in a program of more than 2048 files

The runtime got a source position as (file << 20 | line, col) in two
ints. From file index 2048 on, the first is negative, and AYE_FILE read
aye_files[] at a negative index: the report of a failed check crashed in
strlen (SIGSEGV, nothing on stderr) or printed another string. Dweller
has 2738 files; its weekly conformance run of 2026-11-09 shows it as
exit -11 on webaudio and WebGL 2 pages (Dweller Q1.12).

The file index is now in the upper 16 bits of the column argument
(AYE_FILE, AYE_COL), as wide as Span::file; a column past 65535 is
reported as 65535.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
